        <briefdescription>
<para>Runs the epochs of <computeroutput>runTable</computeroutput> and writes the report. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The paths of <computeroutput>runTable</computeroutput> resolve against the folder of the manifest. When the <computeroutput>baseline</computeroutput> cell names a file that does not exist, the function fails before it runs any epoch. An empty <computeroutput>baseline</computeroutput> cell means no baseline. Each epoch runs the <computeroutput><ref refid="juce__UnityPluginInterface_8h_1a485dc2a0e5ed7da3d9f826367b36ee55a6440030ae8284cee96c1c88b356c45a7" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/tagfile.xml">command</ref></computeroutput> through <ref refid="class_benchmark_1a8b4bab8a038fba5d18366ba23e32923f" kindref="member">Benchmark::runEpoch()</ref> and reads the <computeroutput>samples</computeroutput> file through <ref refid="class_benchmark_1a54e743cd8ac66536390608cc09aa355e" kindref="member">Benchmark::addEpoch()</ref>. The function runs <computeroutput>epochs</computeroutput> epochs, then passes the profiles to <ref refid="struct_processor_1aa277929ee4d6480d62fa48d2dd5f2a6c" kindref="member">writeReport()</ref>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>runTable</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_processor_1a6ace9660425275f32080160c0ae88b2b" kindref="member">run</ref></computeroutput> table of the manifest. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><ref refid="classjuce_1_1Result_1ac2133128eeba510367bfe1b83383ae0f" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/tagfile.xml">juce::Result::ok()</ref> when every epoch and the report succeed, or the first failure. A missing baseline gives <computeroutput>not found: \&lt;baseline path\&gt;</computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
